From: vps-ssh-launcher maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Priority reclaim in WorkBuddy account picking (0.9.84)
Source: https://github.com/mmqz/cpa-multi-plugins/tree/v0.8.92 (workbuddy 0.9.82)
        + repo patch stack through 0.9.84 (selected-account, account-failover,
        exhausted-pool-delegate, 11-128 stringified cooling, intl system-first)
Source tree: /root/cpa-workbuddy-0984-20261102-build on bwg (VERSION 0.9.84);
tree verified faithful to production by built-artifact SHA256 equality with the
deployed workbuddy.so (bbf57c0ad33a6de33507de9c20fedc505edfa93fecbee05507834255f1e53368).
Tarball SHA256 not retained by this patch; re-derive from the tree when in doubt.
Consumer: manual WorkBuddy build for CPA v8.0.51; MIT, license retained in source.
Motivation: pickActiveAuth sticky never reclaims after a transient cooldown
window (6004 model-level throttling cascades ratcheted serving onto a
lower-priority account until its credits ran out). With INTL-first filename
ordering the sticky broke the mandated serving order exactly when upstream
recovered. Patch makes every pick serve the sorted-first live candidate; the
all-exhausted fallback (keep current, else first) is unchanged.
Behavior note: the panel pin (使用中) now defers to any earlier live account;
it still governs the all-exhausted fallback and the panel display.
Retire when upstream provides an equivalent priority-reclaim selection mode
(proposed upstream as mmqz/cpa-multi-plugins#71).

diff --git a/plugins/workbuddy/active_auth.go b/plugins/workbuddy/active_auth.go
--- a/plugins/workbuddy/active_auth.go
+++ b/plugins/workbuddy/active_auth.go
@@ -65,14 +65,12 @@
 	}

 	cur := getActiveAuthID()
-	// Keep current selection if it's still a live candidate AND not disabled/exhausted.
-	if cur != "" {
-		if c, ok := byID[cur]; ok && !c.Disabled && !c.Exhausted {
-			return cur
-		}
-	}
-
-	// Selection is gone, disabled or exhausted — pick next non-disabled non-exhausted, else first.
+	// Priority reclaim (vps-launcher 2026-11-02): every pick serves the
+	// sorted-first live candidate, so a higher-priority account takes over
+	// as soon as it recovers — a cooldown window no longer ratchets the
+	// selection onto a lower-priority sticky account until credits run out.
+	// The panel pin therefore defers to any earlier live account; it still
+	// governs the all-exhausted fallback below.
 	var next string
 	for _, c := range candidates {
 		if !c.Disabled && !c.Exhausted {
